Mitcad's patch to OCCT 8.0.1, under OCCT's licence:
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Fillets: the end of an open stripe whose contact runs along a whole edge
of the face it consumes (patch 0014) becomes that edge's vertex, and so
does the stripe's point there, everywhere in the DS.

E.g. a fin 1.5 thick standing on a wall, its top and bottom flush with the
wall's: the edges round one side rounded with 0.75 (a tangent chain round
the fin's rounded outer corners), then those round the other side with
0.75. The second rounding's contacts on the fin's top and bottom run along
the whole edges the first one left there, up to the wall. 0014 made those
contacts' ends the edges' vertices (ChFiDS_CommonPoint::SetVertex), but at
the stripe's start and end the stripe kept the index of the point it had
made there (0321 replaced it for closed stripes only). ChFi3d_FilDS takes
the kind of the stripe's end from its common point, now a vertex, so it
put the point's index into the DS as a vertex's: with OCCT's exceptions
off (release builds), ChFi3d_Builder::Compute read and updated the
tolerance of the DS's shape of that index as a vertex's (here the solid's
and a face's TShape), past the end of the object, corrupting the heap; the
build then failed (TopoDS_Builder::Add) and the process crashed later
freeing shapes or measuring them. Now the stripe's index there is the
vertex's for open stripes too, and the curves and edges the DS already has
at the old point (the end's) are put at the vertex (the new
ChFi3d_StripeEndAtVertex). The fin builds, valid, each side's rounding
taking off the same volume.
